#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:1
msgid "How to start LLVM Social in your town"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:3
msgid ""
"Here are several ideas you can take into account when designing your "
"specific LLVM Social."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:6
msgid ""
"Before you start, it is essential to make sure that the meetup is as "
"welcoming as any other event related to LLVM. Therefore you shall follow "
"LLVM's [Code of Conduct](https://llvm.org/docs/CodeOfConduct.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:10
msgid ""
"Other than that - your mileage may vary. Please adapt your social to what "
"works best for your specific situation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:13
msgid "General suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:15
msgid ""
"We highly recommend that you join the official LLVM meetup organization. In "
"addition to covering the cost of the meetup, all LLVM meetups are advertised "
"together and easily found by potential attendees. Please contact "
"[tanyalattner@llvm.org](mailto:tanyalattner@llvm.org) for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:19
msgid ""
"Beware of cultural differences: what works well in one region may not work "
"in other part of the world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:21
msgid ""
"Do not be alone to organize the meetup. Try to work with a couple other "
"organizers. This is more motivating as an organizer, and this makes the "
"meetup more resilient over time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:24
msgid ""
"Each event can have a different form such as a social event, or a hackathon/"
"workshop, or a 'mini-conference' with one or more talks. You do not have to "
"stick to one format forever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:27
msgid ""
"Whatever format you choose, [LLVM Weekly](http://llvmweekly.org/) is an "
"excellent topic starter: go through the 3-4 recent LLVM Weekly posts and "
"prepare a list of the most interesting/notable news and discuss them with "
"the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:32
msgid "Advertisement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:34
msgid "Try to advertise via similar meetups/user groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:35
msgid ""
"Advertise your meetup on the mailing lists (llvm-dev, cfe-dev, lldb-"
"dev, ...). Feel free to post to all of them, or at least to llvm-dev. But as "
"these mailing lists have high traffic and some LLVM developers are not very "
"active on them, you may reach more interested people using the mailing "
"feature from meetup.com."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:40
msgid ""
"Advertise the meetup on Twitter and mention [@llvmweekly](http://twitter.com/"
"llvmweekly) and [@llvmorg](http://twitter.com/llvmorg)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:43
msgid "Announce the next meetup in advance, and remind in one week or so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:45
msgid "Tech talks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:47
msgid ""
"It’s a great idea to have several talks scheduled for several upcoming "
"meetups to get the ball rolling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:49
msgid ""
"Keep looking for speakers far in advance, ideally you should have 2-3 "
"speakers ready in the pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:51
msgid ""
"Try to record the talks if possible. It adds visibility to the meetup and "
"just a good idea in general. Any modern smartphone or tablet should work, "
"but you can also get a camera. Though, it is recommended to get an external "
"microphone for better sound."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:56
msgid "Where to host the meetup?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:58
msgid "Look around for bars/café with projectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:59
msgid "Talk to tech companies in the area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:60
msgid ""
"Some co-working spaces provide their facilities for non-profit (i.e., you do "
"not charge attendees any fees) meetups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:62
msgid "Ask nearby universities or university departments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:64
msgid "How to pick the date?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:66
msgid ""
"Make sure you do not clash with the similar meetups in the city (e.g., C++ "
"user groups)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:68
msgid ""
"Prefer not to have a meetup the same week when the other similar meetups "
"happen (e.g., it’s not a good idea to have LLVM meetup on Thursday after C++ "
"meetup on Wednesday)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:71
msgid ""
"Meetups on weekends may attract people who live far away from the city, but "
"the people who live in the city may not attend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../MeetupGuidelines.md:73
msgid ""
"Make a poll, but beware that not every responder will join (we had ~20 votes "
"on the poll, while only ~8 people attended)."
msgstr ""
